{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra","id":1104465,"title":"Sealing off the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-16T13:44:27-07:00","id":1104465,"title":"Sealing off the Umbra","content":"Anyone ever try sealing off the Umbra as if the Avatar Storm affected the Garou as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13458-adamg","name":"AdamG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:27:32-07:00","id":1104526,"title":"","content":"Um... not like the Avatar Storm. It would be magnitudes more disruptive to the game than the Avatar Storm was, and just messes up way too much. Also, the Avatar Storm didn't &quot;seal&quot; off the Umbra, it made it more dangerous to access, and made sources of safe access more valuable. The Avatar Storm with WtA also doesn't have the impact of trying to cut off the younger (PC) mages from the older leadership hiding in the Umbra to avoid Paradox. The Elders of the Garou Nation still live on Earth and can be readily accessed without the Umbra.<br /> <br /> I've certainly dealt with such things on a small/short scale. There's powers in the books just for doing so (like the Philodox Rite in Book of Auspices). There's plenty of fun in something more localized as an issue that the Sept needs to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T23:36:48-07:00","id":1104625,"title":"","content":"Sealing off the Umbra = the game is over, everyone go home, the Weaver won and now the cosmos is going to slowly die, possibly like in Uzumaki due to the Wyrm thrashing around..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:00:14-07:00","id":1104639,"title":"","content":"Well, as I remember there was certainly an option in the books to make Avatar Storm affect everyone, not just mages. But garou would have it a lot easier as they can soak aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T08:51:55-07:00","id":1104735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104639#post1104639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I remember there was certainly an option in the books to make Avatar Storm affect everyone, not just mages. But garou would have it a lot easier as they can soak aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mage runs off a completely different assumption of cosmology where the Umbra is something it takes some time to work into. Werewolf has it as an integral part of an animistic world where, without its spirit, something ends up broken and ruined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T10:14:12-07:00","id":1104765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104735#post1104735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Mage runs off a completely different assumption of cosmology where the Umbra is something it takes some time to work into. Werewolf has it as an integral part of an animistic world where, without its spirit, something ends up broken and ruined.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b??? What? Umbra is the same for both splats, mages just work more in different parts of it, while Garou use middle umbra in general. Even so, Werewolf cosmology is standard for Verbena and Dremspeakers (and many, many others). What are you talking about? Avatar Storm doesn't meat middle world is cut off from umbra, it even flays the gauntlet! The problem is PC's can't get through to the other side without being lashed by hurricane made of fragmented souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T10:26:36-07:00","id":1104770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104765#post1104765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b??? What? Umbra is the same for both splats, mages just work more in different parts of it, while Garou use middle umbra in general. Even so, Werewolf cosmology is standard for Verbena and Dremspeakers (and many, many others). What are you talking about? Avatar Storm doesn't meat middle world is cut off from umbra, it even flays the gauntlet! The problem is PC's can't get through to the other side without being lashed by hurricane made of fragmented souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the games treat it very differently, starting from the fact that every last Garou can inherently Step Sideways, but mages have to wait until they have a high rating in Spirit to do the same. There's also how outer space is entirely physical in Werewolf, but in Mage, going past the asteroid belt puts you into the Deep Umbra... which is not even remotely the same between the two games, and never really has been, since Werewolf has a distinct Aetherial Realm apart from physical outer space and the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Then we get back to the difference between what the two games consider true reality. For Werewolf, it's spirits all the way down. For Mage, it's largely about beliefs held by humans. The two diverge even further on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:02:40-07:00","id":1104786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104770#post1104770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the games treat it very differently, starting from the fact that every last Garou can inherently Step Sideways, but mages have to wait until they have a high rating in Spirit to do the same. There's also how outer space is entirely physical in Werewolf, but in Mage, going past the asteroid belt puts you into the Deep Umbra... which is not even remotely the same between the two games, and never really has been, since Werewolf has a distinct Aetherial Realm apart from physical outer space and the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Then we get back to the difference between what the two games consider true reality. For Werewolf, it's spirits all the way down. For Mage, it's largely about beliefs held by humans. The two diverge even further on this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bmost of that has nothing to do with the gauntlet and in general proves nothing of your claims. Have you even read M20? Or about avatar storm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:05:00-07:00","id":1104787,"title":"","content":"The Truth has Arcane and Obfuscate stupendously high.<br /> <br /> Us lowly Forumites don't stand a chance to really find it.<br /> <br /> Thematically it is an interesting story to be told if the storm affects <b>anything</b>.<br /> Of course it is easier for Garou, because they can soak.<br /> On the other hand, Garou have it harder because opting against umbratravel is seldom an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:10:21-07:00","id":1104791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104786#post1104786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bmost of that has nothing to do with the gauntlet and in general proves nothing of your claims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage had a problem with too much far-flung gonzo stuff in the Umbra. Werewolf is extremely down to earth and visceral with its presentation. The effects of trying to close up avenues to the Umbra will be vastly different between the two games, especially since all Garou and Fera are half-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:33:25-07:00","id":1104823,"title":"","content":"Even if you directly translate the Avatar Storm to WtA with something to make it threatening to Garou (the current roll for damage from the Avatar storm for them would be zero dice).<br /> <br /> As well, it really isn't that big of a deal because the Garou are already far more obsessed with their Caerns than mages are with Nodes. The Caern of any decently sized Sept is already an easy access to the Umbra around the Avatar Storm (Shallowings ignore the Avatar Storm completely, and are a common feature in Caerns but rare in Nodes, and any Caern without one could temporarily have one via Rites very easily). As well you have Totem spirits at both the pack and Sept level to aid in crossing the Gauntlet since in Mage spirits can aid in spreading the damage around and thus make travel less dangerous. Garou have a lot more access to spirit control powers than Mages, either positive ones that rely on ancient pacts, or forced ones like certain Rites and Gifts. Unlike Dreamspeakers that would have to be very careful in how they treat most spirits, the majority of Garou can easily summon up a Weaver spirit and have it be a shield without serious issues. It could even become common practice in certain Tribes to &quot;put Banes to good use,&quot; by binding them into talens instead of destroying them just to let them get shredded by the Avatar Storm for the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:40:12-07:00","id":1104825,"title":"","content":"That would be a hilarious use of Banes. Anyway, it would not matter if the Avatar Storm did effect Garou. It would just do 0 dice of aggravated damage because Garou have 0 Arete and 0 Permanent Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:49:37-07:00","id":1104828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104825#post1104825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a hilarious use of Banes. Anyway, it would not matter if the Avatar Storm did effect Garou. It would just do 0 dice of aggravated damage because Garou have 0 Arete and 0 Permanent Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea would be that if <b>anything</b> is affected by the storm, that the storm gets some dice against beings without Arete/Paradox.<br /> Otherwise it would be pointless, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T13:10:45-07:00","id":1104835,"title":"","content":"Why? It would not effect Spirits, Wraiths, Kuei-jin, or Kindred using Astral Projection. It sucks for Mages, but it is good to see Mages take it up the rear once and a while. And it is not like clever Mages could not avoid the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T15:29:38-07:00","id":1104881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104465-sealing-off-the-umbra?p=1104835#post1104835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It would not effect Spirits, Wraiths, Kuei-jin, or Kindred using Astral Projection. It sucks for Mages, but it is good to see Mages take it up the rear once and a while. And it is not like clever Mages could not avoid the damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I would go the route of sealing of the umbra, I would say that it makes sense to change the mechanics of the storm so that it affects anyone and anything. Yes even spirits.<br /> Even inert matter/ephemera.<br /> I wouldn't want to roll actual damage against all, but I bet I could cook up something appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T18:06:03-07:00","id":1104940,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse already had a scenario for the Umbra being sealed off. The Umbra being cut off was literally an end game event.<br /> <br /> Either way, as pointed out, the Garou would have ways around the Avatar Storm via their Caerns and Rites. So that particular mechanic is less absolute/game changing. There biggest outcome I think it's just having Garou about Sidestepping unprepared. Even them, they have a decent chance of soaking the damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}